//! Unicode Collation Algorithm data version 17.0.0.
//!
//! # What is here and what is not
//!
//! Every single-codepoint entry, as weights at three levels: primary is the
//! letter, secondary the accent, tertiary the case. Comparing at fewer levels is
//! what a case- or diacritic-insensitive collator does.
//!
//! Not here: the 964 *contractions*, sequences of several codepoints that
//! collate as one unit — Danish `aa` sorting as `å` is the usual example. They
//! need a longest-match scan over the input rather than a per-codepoint lookup,
//! and the comparison here does not do one, so those sequences compare as their
//! parts. Counted rather than silently dropped.

/// One codepoint's weights: primary, secondary, tertiary.
pub type Weights = (u16, u16, u16);

